    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0171" n="63" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg63"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-25"><hi rendition="#italic">October 25,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Gresham acknowledges Mr. Thompson’s telegram of the 24th, and remarks that
                    recognition by the United States of the insurgents as belligerents would be an
                    unfriendly act toward Brazil and a gratuitous demonstration of moral support to
                    the rebellion, the insurgents having not, apparently, up to date established and
                    maintained apolitical organization which would justify such recognition on the
                    part of the United States. He instructs him to observe, until further advised,
                    the attitude of an indifferent spectator, and communicates to him the
                    President’s expectation that he will transmit to the Department all information
                    bearing on events transpiring at Rio de Janeiro and other ports of Brazil and
                    espouse the cause of neither side.</p>
            </div>
